From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: d2d1: effect bounds, CombineWithGeometry and Widen

The next three walls Paint.NET hit, drawing its first controls:

 - GetImageLocalBounds of an effect returned E_NOTIMPL. An effect's
   rectangle now comes from its transform graph: each node maps its
   inputs' rectangles to its output's -- draw and compute transforms
   through MapInputRectsToOutputRect (after PrepareForRender), offset,
   bounds adjustment, border (infinite) and blend (union) transforms here,
   effects used as nodes recursively -- up to the output node, or the
   passthrough input. A built-in effect's comes from its properties (crop,
   blurs and shadow by three deviations, morphology, scale, 2D affine
   transform, flood/tile/border/turbulence infinite, composites the union,
   bitmap source its bitmap, the rest their first input). A command list's
   extent is not tracked (infinite). GetImageWorldBounds is the local
   bounds under the transform. ID2D1Effect::SetInput takes NULL.
 - CombineWithGeometry (all geometry types) was a stub. Both geometries
   are flattened; the plane is cut into slabs at every vertex and edge
   crossing; in each slab the edges' order and each geometry's winding
   (by its fill mode) give the intervals where the union, intersection,
   xor or difference is filled; intervals between the same two edges in
   consecutive slabs grow into one polygon. The result's polygons do not
   overlap.
 - Widen was a stub: each flattened segment's rectangle, the joins
   (miter within the limit, else bevel; round) and caps (flat, square,
   round, triangle), turned the same way, united the same way. Dashes are
   not applied.

Gate: test/d2dfx-gate.sh (a blur's bounds, the four combinations' and a
widened square's areas). d2d1:d2d1 0 failures (todo_wine removed from the
crop effect's bounds).
